+From 1afdeaa0ad68cbf37e64b8927ccbfb250cf2b1b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
+Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:42:37 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH 2/2] streamaggr: emit a zero when an output expires on
+ staleness
+
+Adds the reset_marker_on_stale aggregation option, off by default, which
+applies to the total and total_prometheus outputs only: when every input
+of an output series has stopped reporting for longer than
+staleness_interval and the state is dropped, a zero-valued sample is
+emitted first.
+
+Without it, a new input accumulates from a small value after the state is
+gone, and if that value is not below the one from before the expiry,
+increase() cannot see the counter reset and undercounts. The zero makes
+the reset explicit.
+
+This is only correct when the input really does restart from zero after
+the gap, as it does when a scrape target deletes idle series. If the
+expiry was caused by a scrape outage longer than staleness_interval, the
+value from before the gap is counted twice after recovery. Configuring the
+option without a total or total_prometheus output fails to load.
