+From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
+Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:41:07 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH 17/17] lib/streamaggr: benchmark the push path on the shape
+ ACG deploys
+
+The existing push benchmark sets by: [job], which sends ten of its twelve
+labels into the input part of a sample's key. The config this fork is deployed
+under sets neither by nor without -- the labels the aggregation must not group
+by are removed with drop_input_labels -- so aggregateOnlyByTime is on, every
+remaining label goes to the output part, and the input part is empty.
+
+That matters for reading the numbers on 08f4b377d, which stopped building the
+input part unless an output reads it: 119.9ms against 69.7ms on the by: [job]
+shape, and on this one the difference is inside the noise, with runs of a
+single build spread over 92ms to 107ms. There is nothing for it to save here,
+because there was nothing in the input part to begin with. The change is worth
+having for configurations that do use by or without; it is not where this
+deployment's time goes.
+
+Measured by checking out the parent commit's lib/streamaggr rather than
+stashing: the change was already committed, so a stash had nothing to take and
+both sides of the first attempt ran the same build.
