+From 6e1524e8b0caedf01091e9fc9fb5b4435f5ea295 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
+Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 04:22:40 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH 19/19] lib/streamaggr: dedup was losing every input series but
+ one
+
+An adversarial review found that the change which stopped building the input
+part of a sample's key read aggrOutputs.useInputKey, and that field is already
+false for a second, unrelated reason: dedup_interval > 0. The narrowing loop
+that decides "no output reads the input part" only runs when dedup is off, so
+the dedup case was never meant to be covered -- but compressLabels read the
+same flag for both meanings.
+
+With dedup on, dedupAggrShard keys its map on the now input-less key, so every
+input series in an output group shares one entry. Three pods each reporting 1
+through `interval: 1m / dedup_interval: 30s / without: [pod] / sum_samples`
+summed to 1 instead of 3. total and rate got a single shared per-input state,
+and count_series would always report 1.
+
+The two questions are now two fields: useInputKey, untouched, and
+buildInputKey, which is true unless dedup is off and no configured output
+reads the input part. The test drives both dedup settings through the existing
+stale-scenario harness; putting the shared flag back fails the dedup case.
+
+Also from the same review:
