++Subject: [PATCH 4/4] streamaggr: emit a leading zero for a new output under
++ reset_marker_on_stale
++
++The previous patch only emits a zero when an output expires on staleness.
++When vmagent restarts or crashes and loses the aggregation state there is
++no zero at all: the output stopped at X before the restart, a low-traffic
++key gets one request afterwards, the new output starts from a small Y, and
++where Y >= X increase() cannot see the reset across the two stretches and
++loses X. Any long window, daily or monthly, runs into this.
++
++With reset_marker_on_stale on, a newly created output state now emits a
++zero one interval before its first visible flush. Whether the previous
++stretch ended in an ordinary expiry, which already has its zero, an
++ordinary restart or a crash, the new stretch starts from an explicit zero.
