++From b2469ee1896f2590bccc44a7a8871435170c0f77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
++Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:17:14 -0700
++Subject: [PATCH 7/7] streamaggr: do not use a future timestamp for the
++ shutdown flush
++
++With flush_on_shutdown, the flush at shutdown used the next flush
++boundary, which lies in the future. With reset_marker_on_stale on, the
++aggregator that comes back emits its leading zero at its own start time,
++the old process's shutdown flush lands after that, and increase() sees
++X -> 0 -> X and counts X twice. End to end, with the sidecar reporting
++increments into sum_samples_total, the vmagent restart window overcounted
++by 12%.
++
++With reset_marker_on_stale on, the shutdown flush timestamp is now no
++later than the current time.
