++From b1b1cb641d805e3ac7b651cf355d5f4b4331b8d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
++Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:45:41 -0700
++Subject: [PATCH 12/12] lib/storage: make TestStorageDeletePendingSeries
++ independent of the time zone
++
++The test walks ten months from the epoch, and reads back the per-day index
++entry at each one. It derives those months from time.Unix(0, 0) in local
++time, steps forward a month at a time when writing rows, and backwards a
++month at a time when rewriting them after the delete.
++
++West of UTC the epoch is the 31st of December, and AddDate normalizes the
++31st of February to the 3rd of March, so the forward walk drifts -- Jan 1,
++Feb 1, Mar 4, Apr 4, May 3 -- while the backward walk, starting from a
++single nine-month jump, does not. The two land on different days, so the
++rows go into per-day index entries the assertions never look at, and only
++the first month, where the two agree, comes back:
++
++  unexpected labels count; got 1; want 10
++
++In UTC the epoch is the 1st, no normalization happens, and both walks
++agree, which is why CI does not see this.
++
++  before  UTC ok, Europe/Berlin ok, Asia/Shanghai ok, America/Los_Angeles FAIL
++  after   all four ok, and Pacific/Honolulu at UTC-10 as well
++
++Reverting either .UTC() alone brings the failure back, at 7 of 10 and 2 of
++10 months respectively, so both are doing work.
++
++The storage itself is not involved: the same failure reproduces on a
++pristine v1.126.0 worktree, and on v1.127.0, v1.128.0, v1.129.0 and
++v1.129.1.
