++From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
++Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 01:29:05 -0700
++Subject: [PATCH 13/13] lib/streamaggr: pin what a type-label selector takes
++
++The aggregation config we recommend for the delta SDK keys on a label
++carrying the metric's type, so that a metric added later needs no change to
++the config. That rests on one selector detail which is easy to get wrong
++and which nothing reports: a matcher reads an absent label as empty, so a
++negative match on the type also takes every sample that carries no type at
++all, and sum_samples_total then adds each cumulative value it sees on top
++of the last.
++
++The test asserts all three selectors against a counter, a gauge and a
++sample with no type label, the wrong one included, so that the emptiness
++condition cannot be dropped from the config as a simplification.
