+++Subject: [PATCH 11/16] promutil: benchmark what an exposer's label ordering
+++ costs Sort
+++
+++A sidecar that renders an extra label after the metric's own labels, which
+++Write hands out sorted, leaves one name out of place at the end of every
+++series. Sort then has to carry it back to where it belongs.
+++
+++  generation appended   70.5 ns/op
+++  generation sorted     47.4 ns/op
+++
+++Medians of three at 3s. On the API-key label set that is 23 ns per series,
+++or 0.21 s/min of one vmagent's CPU at 9.1M samples/min -- real, and well
+++under what a system-level measurement of the same run can resolve.
+++
+++The benchmark checks that its two inputs really are the two orderings
+++before timing them: built by hand, they are easy to get identical, and a
+++benchmark comparing a thing with itself reports no difference just as
+++convincingly as one comparing two things that are the same.
